# Docker build context for the ussdgw images.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT
# ---------------------------------------
# Docker reads exactly ONE ignore file per build, and it is chosen by path — not
# by search: `<context-root>/.dockerignore`, or `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`.
# Every image here is built from the repository root with
# `docker build -f docker/<x>/Dockerfile .`, so the only file Docker will ever
# consult is THIS one. The previous `docker/.dockerignore` matched neither rule
# and was therefore completely inert: the daemon received a 431 MB context plus
# a 2.9 GB `.git`, together with `build/digicom-secrets-*.txt` and every
# `ss7-digicom*.json`. `docker/.dockerignore` has been deleted rather than
# renamed: its contents contradicted the Dockerfiles (it excluded `dist/lib/`,
# `dist/quarkus/`, `dist/app/`, `dist/.baked-db-kind` and `dist/*.jar`, which are
# precisely what `docker/ussdgw/Dockerfile` COPYs), so enabling it as-is would
# have failed the build instead of shrinking it.
#
# THE RULE FOR THIS FILE
# ----------------------
# Ignore everything except what a Dockerfile actually COPYs. `docker/ussdgw/
# Dockerfile` copies dist/{ussdgw-app.jar,quarkus-run.jar,lib,quarkus,app/
# html,run.sh,.baked-db-kind} and out/BUILD-INFO.json; `docker/build/Dockerfile`
# copies docker/build and docker/sources.lock; `docker/nginx/Dockerfile` copies
# docker/nginx/*.conf. Every ignore block below is verified against those COPY
# instructions — if you add a COPY, re-check this file in the same commit.

# --- Git and editor noise (2.9 GB of history, never needed in a layer) -------
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
*.iml
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
.worktrees/

# --- Maven / build outputs that are not the shipped dist --------------------
# NOTE: `dist/` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the runtime image's payload.
# The maven reactor's own output tree is `target/`, not `dist/`.
target/
**/target/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# --- Secrets and operator state — must never enter a layer -----------------
# `.env` holds rendered secrets; the digicom overlay config holds carrier
# secrets (DIAL string, AS URLs, admin keys). Only `dist/configs/` is baked,
# and only its lab-safe subset, via `docker/ussdgw/Dockerfile`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
build/digicom-secrets-*.txt
build/.digicom-rotate.env
build/application-digicom.properties
build/systemd/
configs/digicom/
ss7-digicom-balance.json
ss7-digicom*.json
build/ss7-digicom-balance.json

# --- Runtime state (recreated on every boot; never from a build) -------------
data/
logs/
docker/logs/
dist/data/
dist/logs/
*.log
*.pcap
*.mv

# --- Lab tooling, docs and tests the images do not need --------------------
# `dist/app/html/` IS needed (the operator UI) and is not matched by these.
docs/
plan.md
tools/
docker/capacity/
docker/README.md
# Sources are bind-mounted at build time by docker/build/run-build.sh, never
# baked, so a Dockerfile never needs the Java sources themselves.
src/
